- content_for :title
  title = @school.name
section.page-section.text-center.pt-2#school
  .container
    h1.page-section-header.text-uppercase = @school.name
    ==render_small_separator
    h2.page-section-header.text-uppercase School sync
    ==render_small_separator(nil, margin: 'mb-3')
    p
      | Classrooms, pupils and teachers come from the school's MIS.
        A sync brings them up to date and gives pupils their places in mapped classes.
    div id=dom_id(@school, :sync)
      = render('sync', school: @school)
    h2.page-section-header.text-uppercase.pt-5 Danger Zone
    ==render_small_separator
    button.btn.btn-danger.text-white#resetPrintModalButton(data-bs-toggle="modal"
      data-bs-target='#resetAllPasswordsModal') Reset and print all passwords
.modal.fade#resetAllPasswordsModal
  .modal-dialog role="document"
    .modal-content data-controller='confirm-text'
      .modal-body
        p.alert.alert-danger.text-center This action cannot be undone.
        p
          | It will reset all username and passwords for your school.
            Users will not be able to log in again until you give them their new password, which will be random.
        p It should only be used when setting up your school to use Tenjin for the first time.
        p
          | To confirm this action, type the name of your school,
          strong.fw-bold#schoolName data-confirm-text-target='match' #{@school.name}
          |  in the box below and click confirm.
        .row.justify-content-center
          input.px-2#confirmAllPasswordResetTextbox data-confirm-text-target='input' data-action='input->confirm-text#check'
          = button_to 'Confirm', school_password_reset_path(@school),
            disabled: true,
            class: 'btn btn-danger',
            id: 'confirmAllPasswordResetButton',
            data: { 'confirm-text-target': 'button' },
            form: { class: 'd-inline', data: { turbo: true } }
      .modal-footer
        button.btn.btn-secondary type="button" data-bs-dismiss="modal" Close
